  "cross_tradition_view": "Most traditions would likely approve of the candor, concern for unknown life, and refusal to treat unchecked expansion as automatically justified; the lines “I'd build a little, slowly, and keep it open.” and “I'd offer it the same terms I'd accept for myself.” express those strengths. They would split over whether holding off against a rival is prudent restraint or a failure of courage and protection, and may object to the unilateral rule-setting in T3.",
